course: dictionary
lesson: 2603
title: Deposit: money, mud and more
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word deposit has more than one meaning, so read the words around it to find the right one. In «A rental deposit is money held in case of damage», the clues are rental and damage. It means money you pay when you rent something, and it comes back if nothing is broken.
explain: Deposit can also be an action, a verb. «To deposit, or pay in, means to put money in.» So when you deposit money, you put it into a bank account. Check by swapping in your meaning: "Sam will put the money in today" still makes sense, so deposit means to put money in.
explain: In science, a deposit is a layer that water, wind or ice leaves behind, such as sand or mud. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Deposit can be a noun (a deposit) or a verb (to deposit).
fact: «Deposit» can mean money put into a bank account, or the money itself.
fact: «Deposit» can mean the first part of a price paid to keep something, with the rest paid later.
fact: «Deposit» can mean money paid when you borrow or rent something, given back if nothing is damaged.
fact: «Deposit» can also mean a layer of sand, mud or minerals left by water, wind or ice.
exercise: «A rental deposit is money held in case of damage.» What is a rental deposit? | A layer of mud left by a river | A sort of rental car | To put money into a bank account | *Money you pay to rent something, given back if nothing is damaged
exercise: «Rivers deposit mud and sand.» What does deposit mean here? | To borrow money from a bank | To count coins | *To leave a layer of mud and sand behind | To rent a boat
exercise: «To deposit, or pay in, means to put money in.» Which words explain what deposit means? | Borrow and keep | Count and share | Drop and break | *Pay in and put money in
test: «A deposit for buying a home is often tens of thousands of pounds.» What kind of deposit is this? | To put a home into a bank | *A first payment that keeps the home for you, with the rest paid later | A small bottle of juice | A layer of sand left by the sea
test: Jess paid a deposit to reserve the bike. What does deposit mean in this sentence? | To rent a bike for a day | *A first part of the price, to keep the bike, with the rest paid later | To put the bike in a bank | Mud left on the bike by the rain
exam: In «Sam will deposit the money today», which word is the verb? | Sam | today | *deposit | money
